--TEST--
A continuation reference is a URL the server chose, so `references()` returns `tainted string` values and a plain `array<string>` does not take them — ADR 0278 § 5 and `rule:security/tainted-qualifier`
--FILE--
<?nvs
class Referrals {
    public static function of(Core\Ldap\Entries $entries): array<string> {
        array<string> $urls = $entries->references();
        return $urls;
    }
}
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0401]: expected `array<string>`, found `array<tainted string>`
%A
error: aborting due to 1 error
